ce reflects the pass-through income we expect as a result of the real estate tax increases I mentioned earlier.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/01/28/equity-lifestyle-properties-inc-els-q4-2019-earnin.aspx"},{"c":"ELS 2019 Q4","e":"els","d":"2020-01-28","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Samir Khanal","x":"Just trying to see if there is a sort of pass-through to the customer or anything that we're missing here?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/01/28/equity-lifestyle-properties-inc-els-q4-2019-earnin.aspx"},{"c":"ELS 2020 Q1","e":"els","d":"2020-04-21","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"John Pawlowski","x":"But I guess the quick -- or just maybe the succinct question is, just given the sheer number of layoffs you see today, is it reasonable to expect that your family communities see some diminution in occupancy?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/04/21/equity-lifestyle-properties-inc-els-q1-2020-earnin.aspx"},{"c":"ELS 2020 Q1","e":"els","d":"2020-04-21","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"John Pawlowski","x":"And can you give -- humor us with a rough dollar number of cost savings that you're proactively looking to grab in the back half of this year or early 2021?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/04/21/equity-lifestyle-properties-inc-els-q1-2020-earnin.aspx"},{"c":"ELS 2020 Q1","e":"els","d":"2020-04-21","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Marguerite Nader","x":"We made the decision to withdraw guidance because we are operating under unprecedented conditions and thought it would be more meaningful for us to provide an outlook when there are updates to regulatory protocol.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/04/21/equity-lifestyle-properties-inc-els-q1-2020-earnin.aspx"},{"c":"ELS 2020 Q2","e":"els","d":"2020-07-21","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Paul Seavey","x":"Increases in pass-through and utility income, primarily resulting from pass-throughs of real estate tax increases that were effective in late 2019 were offset by reduced revenue resulting from our suspension of late fees as well as fees related to transient RV state.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/21/equity-lifestyle-properties-inc-els-q2-2020-earnin.aspx"},{"c":"ELS 2020 Q2","e":"els","d":"2020-07-21","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Marguerite Nader","x":"And then John, we also have our -- at the level of Florida, for instance, where we have the ability to pass through real estate taxes.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/21/equity-lifestyle-properties-inc-els-q2-2020-earnin.aspx"},{"c":"ELS 2020 Q4","e":"els","d":"2021-01-26","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Paul Seavey","x":"The pass-through income represents recovery of 2019 tax increases, mainly in Florida, and the utility income increase reflects recovery of increased expense resulting from higher usage in our properties.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/01/26/equity-lifestyle-properties-inc-els-q4-2020-earnin/"},{"c":"ELS 2020 Q4","e":"els","d":"2021-01-26","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Patrick Waite","x":"But the prices have been relatively consistent year-over-year and I would describe them of as having a significant lift, but that is coupled with strong demand and we'll be looking for opportunities to raise prices where we see that opportunity.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/01/26/equity-lifestyle-properties-inc-els-q4-2020-earnin/"},{"c":"ELS 2021 Q1","e":"els","d":"2021-04-20","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Patrick Waite","x":"We're seeing price increases come through on our new home sale prices, but there is also going to be some price impact on the cost of homes as well as potentially timing for delivery.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/20/equity-lifestyle-properties-inc-els-q1-2021-earnin/"},{"c":"ELS 2021 Q3","e":"els","d":"2021-10-19","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Paul Seavey","x":"Core utility and other income was slightly higher than third quarter 2020 and includes utility and pass through income that offset some of our expenses as well as late fees that we reinstated in late 2020 after suspending them earlier in the year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/10/19/equity-lifestyle-properties-inc-els-q3-2021-earnin/"},{"c":"ELS 2026 Q1","e":"els","d":"2026-04-22","l":"tariffs","r":"analyst","s":"Haendel St. Juste","x":"And then the Canadian tariffs kind of went into effect more than a year ago.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/22/els-q1-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"ELS 2026 Q1","e":"els","d":"2026-04-22","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Paul Seavey","x":"…frankly, primarily regulated and some deregulated markets. utility providers in certain states like Florida do have pricing structures with variability clauses that allow them to recapture some portion of their costs if the regulated rates limit their ability to recapture price increases.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/22/els-q1-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"ELS 2026 Q3","e":"els","d":"2026-10-21","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Michael Goldsmith","x":"Do you think this is a concerted effort to retain annual RV customers, or are you losing pricing power?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/10/21/els-els-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"ELS 2026 Q3","e":"els","d":"2026-10-21","l":"guidance","r":"analyst","s":"Jana Galan","x":"On the RV revision for full year, can you help bridge the lower outlook for 4Q, given it appears that 3Q exceeded expectations on annual, seasonal, and transient?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/10/21/els-els-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"}],"trends":{"theater":[[35,1